dynrec: add Alpha backend

Alpha (EV56 and later, BWX) 64-bit backend derived from the sparc64 one,
using the generic hooks. 32bit values are kept sign-extended in registers
as the ABI requires, helpers are called through $27 relative to the
cpu_regs base register. The code cache is placed near the executable
(above it, as Linux puts the stack right below the executable on Alpha).
Memory and stack accesses look up the TLB inline, unaligned reads within
a page use ldq_u/extxl/extxh; branch conditions, the carry into ADC/SBB,
flag-setting ALU operations, shifts and INC/DEC are evaluated inline, block
links are patched to br, jsr/jmp carry target hints. FPU arithmetic, stack
and loads/stores are inline with IEEE software completion (/su), and the C
code is built with -mieee, as masked x87 exceptions must not raise SIGFPE.

Performance on a Digital AlphaPC 164LX (EV56 599 MHz), DOSBox cycles=max,
machine=svga_s3, SB Pro, measured under Xvfb:

  Test                    normal core   dynamic core   speedup
  3DBENCH                  8.4 fps      25.0 fps       2.98x
  Doom -timedemo demo3                  12.8 fps
                                        (5845 rt, 2134 gametics)
  Quake +timedemo demo1                  4.2 fps
                                        (232.8 s, 969 frames)

Signed-off-by: René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

